From 8f2dc934a852c16161a51f1db8515e1d74b3e7db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Crunchtools <noreply@crunchtools.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 04:25:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Honour `pattern` on exception entries

An exception's `pattern` key was dropped by serde, so an entry written for
one finding suppressed every finding of that check in the file. Treat it as
a granular selector: the exception applies only to violations whose item or
message contains the pattern as a literal substring, and it no longer
triggers the file-level skip path.
